export const helpSections=[["h3", "A bookmark is your backup"], ["p", "Kin stores names and birth dates inside the part of the URL after #. Copy or bookmark the full link after every change. An older bookmark remains an older snapshot. Sharing does not create a live sync."], ["h3", "Private by design, readable by anyone with the link"], ["p", "Your family data is decoded on your device. It is not sent to the app’s server. The link is compressed, not encrypted: anyone who receives it can read it. Keep copies somewhere you trust."], ["h3", "Offline, after the first visit"], ["p", "Wait for “Ready for offline” before disconnecting. Calculations, editing, importing and QR generation then work without a connection. Installing is optional. If browser data is cleared or the cache is evicted, reconnect once to reload Kin, then open your saved link. A different device needs its own first online visit."], ["h3", "Which Hijri calendar?"], ["p", "Kin uses a frozen Umm al-Qura month table (AH 1300–1600), so the same date produces the same result across devices. Local moon sightings may differ. Hijri is itself a lunar calendar; other calendar systems can be added later."], ["h3", "What does an exact age mean?"], ["p", "Elapsed calendar years, months and days from the birth date, using today’s local date. Gregorian and Hijri ages can differ; total days lived is the same. Dates change at local midnight; this is date-based, not a sunset or birth-time calculation."], ["p", "For a birthday on a missing date—29 February or day 30 in a shorter Hijri month—we use that month’s last day. A birthday today shows 0 days to go."], ["h3", "Keep links small"], ["p", "Only names, birth dates, original input calendars and stable identifiers are stored. Ages, weekdays and countdowns are calculated. Each link supports up to 150 people. Long links may be truncated by other apps; selective sharing makes smaller links and clearer QR codes."], ["h3", "Merge without losing people"], ["p", "Existing identifiers prevent duplicates. Matching names and birth dates are also recognized. Conflicting edits stay yours unless you choose the shared version. Deletions never spread through a merge."], ["h3","A backup that moves with you"], ["p","Use Download backup in the sharing window to save the selected people as a file. Restore it through Merge a link. The file works without the original website address, but you still need a compatible Kin app to read it. Backups are not encrypted; keep them private."], ["h3","Bring birthdays to your calendar"], ["p","Open Birthdays, choose a range and calendar, and use Export calendar. Search limits which people are included. Gregorian birthdays repeat yearly by default; uncheck the repeat option for dated events. February 29 repeats on the last day of February. Hijri birthdays remain dated events in the chosen range. Imports do not sync with Kin; importing again may create duplicates."]];
